{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Load centrality (Goh, Kahng and Kim 2001; Brandes 2008): from every source s, each vertex"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"t ≠ s sends one unit to s along shortest paths, a vertex splitting what reaches it equally"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"among its shortest-path predecessors (each parallel copy one); a vertex’s load is what"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"passes through it as neither end, summed over ordered pairs (s, t). It differs from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"betweenness, which splits in proportion to the number of shortest paths. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"normalized"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"divides by (n − 1)(n − 2); there is no scaling when n ≤ 2, and an unnormalized sum counts"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"both orders of each pair. Self-loops never matter. O(nm)."}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/centrality\/graphprotocols\/graph\/loadcentrality(normalized:)"]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Centrality\/documentation\/Centrality\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/loadCentrality(normalized:)"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Centrality\/documentation\/Centrality","doc:\/\/Centrality\/documentation\/Centrality\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/Centrality\/documentation\/Centrality\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"sections":[],"metadata":{"remoteSource":{"fileName":"Load.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Centrality\/Load.swift#L101"},"extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","role":"symbol","externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P10CentralityE04loadC010normalizedAD0C6ScoresVyAA12DirectedViewVyxGGSb_tF","roleHeading":"Instance Method","symbolKind":"method","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "